      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="615" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding the phosphopantothenoylcysteine decarboxylase (PPCDC) was isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; and recombinantly expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. The molecular function was shown to liberate carbon dioxide forming 4&apos;-phosphopantetheine |CITS: [12860978]|. The enzyme has been crystallized and its reaction mechanism investigated |CITS: [12614618]|.</Comment>
