    <DataNode elementId="PANTOTHENATE" textLabel="(R)-pantothenate" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="GHOKWGTUZJEAQD-ZETCQYMHSA-M" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="1260" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment>(&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;)-pantothenate, also called vitamin B5, is the amide between |FRAME: L-PANTOATE| and |FRAME: B-ALANINE|. It is a precursor for the synthesis of the 4&apos;-phosphopantetheine moiety of |FRAME:CO-A| and |FRAME: ACP &quot;acyl carrier protein&quot;| in bacteria and eukaryotes. Only plants and microorganisms (including some eukaryotic microbes, such as |FRAME: TAX-4932|) can synthesize pantothenate &lt;i&gt;de novo&lt;/i&gt; - animals require a dietary supplement.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="PANTOTHENATE" />
